**EXPERIMENT 12: Running JUnit Tests with Maven (Including Pass & Fail Cases) – Windows**

---

## 🎯 **Objective**

To execute JUnit test cases using Maven and observe both passing and failing test results.

---

## 🧭 **Startup Guide (Windows System)**

### **Step 0: Open Terminal**

```bat id="x4g1bn"
cd C:\Users\danis\OneDrive\Desktop
```

---

## ⚙️ **Execution Steps**

---

### **Step 1: Create Maven Project**

```bat id="h8h6e3"
mvn archetype:generate -DgroupId=com.example -DartifactId=test-demo -DarchetypeArtifactId=maven-archetype-quickstart -DinteractiveMode=false
```

---

### **Step 2: Move into Project**

```bat id="m8g2w7"
cd test-demo
```

---

### **Step 3: Replace pom.xml (FULL FILE)**

```xml id="q3k2s9"
<project xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0"
         xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
         xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 
         http://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd">

    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>

    <groupId>com.example</groupId>
    <artifactId>test-demo</artifactId>
    <version>1.0-SNAPSHOT</version>

    <dependencies>
        <!-- JUnit 5 -->
        <dependency>
            <groupId>org.junit.jupiter</groupId>
            <artifactId>junit-jupiter</artifactId>
            <version>5.10.0</version>
            <scope>test</scope>
        </dependency>
    </dependencies>

    <build>
        <plugins>
            <!-- Surefire Plugin -->
            <plugin>
                <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
                <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
                <version>3.2.5</version>
            </plugin>
        </plugins>
    </build>

</project>
```

---

### **Step 4: Create Main Class**

```bat id="b7w9p2"
notepad src\main\java\com\example\App.java
```

```java id="c8z5n1"
package com.example;

public class App {

    public int add(int a, int b) {
        return a + b;
    }

    public int multiply(int a, int b) {
        return a * b;
    }
}
```

---

### **Step 5: Create Test Class (3 PASS + 1 FAIL)**

```bat id="a2f9k6"
notepad src\test\java\com\example\AppTest.java
```

```java id="z1x8v3"
package com.example;

import static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.*;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;

public class AppTest {

    App app = new App();

    // ✅ PASS TEST 1
    @Test
    void testAdd() {
        assertEquals(5, app.add(2, 3));
    }

    // ✅ PASS TEST 2
    @Test
    void testMultiply() {
        assertEquals(6, app.multiply(2, 3));
    }

    // ✅ PASS TEST 3
    @Test
    void testAddNegative() {
        assertEquals(1, app.add(3, -2));
    }

    // ❌ FAIL TEST
    @Test
    void testFailure() {
        assertEquals(10, app.add(2, 3)); // wrong expected value
    }
}
```

---

### **Step 6: Run Tests**

```bat id="y5v3k8"
mvn test
```

---

## ❌ **Expected Output (With Failure)**

```text id="u9j4m2"
